{"id": 71511, "date": "2015-02-10T11:00:27", "date_gmt": "2015-02-10T19:00:27", "guid": {"rendered": "https://estreetshuffle.com/?p=71511"}, "modified": "2026-09-06T10:07:55", "modified_gmt": "2026-09-06T17:07:55", "slug": "girlfriend", "status": "publish", "type": "post", "link": "https://estreetshuffle.com/index.php/2015/02/10/girlfriend/", "title": {"rendered": "Girlf(r)iend"}, "content": {"rendered": "<p>&#8220;Girlfriend&#8221; or &#8220;Girl<em>fiend&#8221;?\u00a0</em></p>\n<p>We may never know, because it&#8217;s too late to ask the songwriter, and the titular word never actually appears in the lyrics.</p>\n<div class=\"jetpack-video-wrapper\"><span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"758\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/FIvAe-VAPoE?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></div>\n<p>Still, the mainstream consensus is that Slim Dunlap&#8217;s 1996 infectious album track had a typo in its original release, both on the album cover and the disc itself.</p>\n<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"71513\" data-permalink=\"https://estreetshuffle.com/index.php/2015/02/10/girlfriend/r-3464998-1493976245-8085/#main\" data-orig-file=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?fit=1200%2C1200&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1200,1200\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"R-3464998-1493976245-8085\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?fit=758%2C758&amp;ssl=1\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-71513\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=758%2C758&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"758\" height=\"758\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=1024%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=550%2C550&amp;ssl=1 550w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=600%2C600&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/R-3464998-1493976245-8085.jpg?resize=50%2C50&amp;ssl=1 50w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 758px) 100vw, 758px\" /></p>\n<p>But that wouldn&#8217;t explain while it was still spelled that way on a 2005 re-issue with new album art.</p>\n<p>Or on a 2013 tribute album on the same record label.</p>\n<p>Or why Dunlap himself introduced the song as &#8220;Girlfiend&#8221; when he played it live.</p>\n<audio class=\"wp-audio-shortcode\" id=\"audio-71511-1\" preload=\"none\" style=\"width: 100%;\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"audio/mpeg\" src=\"https://estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Slim-Dunlap-Band-Girlfiend.mp3?_=1\" /><a href=\"https://estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Slim-Dunlap-Band-Girlfiend.mp3\">https://estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Slim-Dunlap-Band-Girlfiend.mp3</a></audio>\n<p>Yet common wisdom says that was a typo, and Bruce Springsteen seems to be among the many who insist on inserting the missing &#8220;r&#8221; in the title, as he did when he revealed an until-then unknown studio cover of the song by the E Street Band during an E Street Radio appearance two days after Dunlap&#8217;s passing.</p>\n<audio class=\"wp-audio-shortcode\" id=\"audio-71511-2\" preload=\"none\" style=\"width: 100%;\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"audio/mpeg\" src=\"https://estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/Video-Project-1.mp3?_=2\" /><a href=\"https://estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/Video-Project-1.mp3\">https://estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/Video-Project-1.mp3</a></audio>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Count me among the few who think Bruce is among the many who simply mis-read the title all these years.</p>\n<p>It&#8217;s still a great cover of a great song by a powerful rock and roll voice who left us too soon.</p>\n<p><strong>Girlfiend<br />\nRecorded:</strong> 2023<br />\n<strong>Never released</strong><br />\n<strong>Never performed</strong></p>\n<p>\u00a9 September 6, 2026</p>\n", "protected": false}, "excerpt": {"rendered": "<p>&#8220;Girlfriend&#8221; or &#8220;Girlfiend&#8221;?\u00a0 We may never know, because it&#8217;s too late to ask the songwriter, and the titular word never actually appears in the lyrics.&hellip;</p>\n", "protected": false}, "author": 1, "featured_media": 71512, "comment_status": "closed", "ping_status": "closed", "sticky": false, "template": "", "format": "st